.gb/

# Quench quality-check cache (cache.bin churns ~1.7MB per run; ka-0000002420).
# The committed ratchet baseline lives in .quench/baseline.json and IS tracked
# (ka-0000002621) — negate it below. A trailing-slash `.quench/` exclude would
# stop git descending into the dir and defeat the negation, so glob the
# contents instead and re-include the one file we track.
.quench/*
!.quench/baseline.json

# Compiled beads-viewer binary (build artifact — never commit; ka-0000004709)
/gardenio/controller/beads-viewer

# Compiled agent-feedback-probe binary — a `go build ./cmd/agent-feedback-probe`
# from gardenio/controller/ (or the shell module's from-source fallback) drops a
# ~64MB binary here (agent-feedback write-path e2e, ka-0000008183). Same
# build-artifact rationale as beads-viewer above; never commit it.
/gardenio/controller/agent-feedback-probe

# Compiled controller binary at repo root — `go build ./gardenio/controller/cmd/controller`
# from the repo root drops a 78MB `controller` binary here. It was accidentally
# committed in the 2026.186.6 release (b68f4e1) and ballooned the shallow-clone
# tip tree, crash-looping agent pods on slow-egress clusters (ka-0000000431).
# Root-anchored so it never shadows the gardenio/controller/ source directory.
/controller

# Compiled beads-viewer binary at repo root — `go build ./gardenio/controller/cmd/beads-viewer`
# from the repo root drops a ~95MB `beads-viewer` binary here. Same build-artifact
# rationale as the /controller entry above; never commit it. Root-anchored so it never
# shadows the gardenio/controller/cmd/beads-viewer/ source directory (ka-0000002684).
/beads-viewer

# Compiled kd CLI binary at repo root — `go build ./cmd/kd` (or a bare `go build`
# run from kbeads/ that lands here) drops a ~48MB `kd` binary here. It was
# accidentally committed in c63dd478c and tripped the 3MB tracked-file guard,
# reddening `make lint` on a clean checkout for everyone (ka-0000001717). Same
# build-artifact rationale as /controller and /beads-viewer above; never commit
# it. Root-anchored so it never shadows any kd source. (kbeads/kd is already
# ignored above for the in-tree build path.)
/kd

# Machine-generated UI-audit captures (screenshots + DOM dumps). Harnesses like
# info-density-audit / maps-beauty / gardeners-camp emit hundreds of multi-MB PNGs
# and DOM .html files under docs/**/captures/ (and, in the legacy info-density
# layout, under docs/info-density/*/inbox/**). Committing them added >1.3GB to the
# shallow-clone tip tree — every agent pod re-downloads it on cold start, blowing
# the coop startup-probe budget on throttled-egress clusters (ka-0000000431).
# The small REPORT.md / metrics.json / verdicts.json beside each dir stay tracked;
# only the heavy binary capture output is ignored. Attach shareable screenshots to
# beads via `gb image upload` (ka-0000002145) instead of committing them.
**/captures/
docs/info-density/**/*.png
docs/info-density/**/*.html
docs/design/**/*.png
docs/design/**/*.jpg
docs/design/**/*.jpeg
docs/design/**/*.webp
docs/design/**/*.gif
__pycache__/

# go build output in the slackmock test module
gardenio/tests/slackmock/slackmock

# git worktrees for isolated sessions (superpowers:using-git-worktrees)
.worktrees/

# Agent-local Claude Code settings (per-pod hook config; never commit changes)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json

# bridge tests built with NewStateManager("") leave a .tmp in the package dir
gardenio/controller/internal/bridge/.tmp

